okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Make the router's Codex completion gate run for code-mode models whose tools arrive as an additional_tools input item, then deploy to robert-ai and local and push nightly."
reported: "User, 2026-09-29: '일단 이거만 수정해서 로버트 세션에 배포, 로컬, 그리고 나이트리시푸'."
diagnosis: "docs/journal/2026/09/29/diagnostics/completion-gate/robert-gate-never-fires.okf"

change:
  gate_precondition: "codex_completion_gate.request_offers_tools(body): top-level tools OR a non-empty additional_tools input item. request_allows_completion_check uses it; router_http buffering condition (was upstream_body.get('tools')) uses it."
  check_body: "completion_check_body: when the request has no top-level tools but an additional_tools item, the private ciel_runtime_confirm_completion tool is appended to that item's 'functions' namespace (created as a plain entry if the namespace is missing) and no top-level tools array is added. The stored/conversation branches keep the modified catalogue item ahead of the nudge. Requests with top-level tools are unchanged."
  why_functions_namespace: "robert-ai rollout: calls to tools in the 'functions' namespace come back without a namespace field (wait x111), clock tools carry namespace 'clock' (sleep x228); completion_confirmed matches by name, so the confirmation is recognised unchanged."

verification:
  unit: "tests/test_codex_completion_gate.py: additional_tools catalogue is checked (empty catalogue and tool_choice none are not); check body adds the private tool to functions only and leaves the original untouched; stored branch keeps the catalogue. tests/test_codex_backend_item_repair.py: router forward_json with a code-mode body sends the check with the tool in input[0] functions, no top-level tools, relays the custom_tool_call and logs codex_completion_gate_continued. All 4 fail on the previous code (3 failures, 1 error) and pass on the new code; targeted run 34 OK; ruff clean."
  e2e_real_codex: "WSL, real codex-cli 0.159.2, model gpt-6-astra with robert's models_cache.json, real router (ciel_runtime.py serve, isolated config, codex-routed) against a stub upstream. old code: 1 upstream request, no gate, Codex printed the text-only reply. new code, confirm scenario: request 2 has tool_choice=required, no top-level tools, functions [..., ciel_runtime_confirm_completion]; log codex_completion_gate_confirmed; Codex printed the original reply. new code, work scenario: the check answered clock.sleep, Codex executed it (request 3 input ends function_call, function_call_output), the next text final was checked again and confirmed; logs codex_completion_gate_continued then codex_completion_gate_confirmed; Codex printed FINAL_AFTER_WORK."
  not_verified_before_deploy: "Whether the real ChatGPT backend accepts the extra function inside additional_tools with tool_choice=required. If it rejects it, the gate logs codex_completion_gate_failed and relays the original reply (existing fallback). To be checked on robert-ai at INFO after deploy."
